{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-001","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 1 — Law of Reversibility","quote_original":"The essence of prayer is faith, but faith must be permeated with understanding to be given that active quality which it does not possess when standing alone.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["UNDERSTANDING"],"tags":["prayer","faith","understanding"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-002","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 1 — Law of Reversibility","quote_original":"If you knew how you would feel were you to realize your objective, then inversely, you would know what state you could realize were you to awaken in yourself such feeling.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","objective","state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-003","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 1 — Law of Reversibility","quote_original":"Assume the feeling of your wish fulfilled and continue feeling that it is fulfilled until that which you feel objectifies itself.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FEELING","FAITH_PRAYER"],"tags":["wish-fulfilled","assumption","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-004","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 2 — Dual Nature of Consciousness","quote_original":"Prayer modifies or completely changes our subconscious assumptions, and a change of assumption is a change of expression.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION","CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["prayer","subconscious","assumption"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-005","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 3 — Imagination and Faith","quote_original":"There must be no conflict in your mind when you are praying. Turn from what is to what ought to be. Assume the mood of fulfilled desire, and by the universal law of reversibility, you will realize your desire.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION","FEELING"],"tags":["prayer","fulfilled-desire","mood"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-006","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 3 — Imagination and Faith","quote_original":"When belief and will are in conflict, belief invariably wins.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["BELIEF"],"tags":["belief","will","conflict"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-007","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 3 — Imagination and Faith","quote_original":"It is not what you want that you attract; you attract what you believe to be true.","primary_topic":"BELIEF","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["belief","desire","assumption"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-008","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 3 — Imagination and Faith","quote_original":"The acceptance of the end wills the means.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FAITH_PRAYER"],"tags":["end","acceptance","means"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-009","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 3 — Imagination and Faith","quote_original":"Imagination is the beginning of the growth of all forms, and faith is the substance out of which they are formed.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["FAITH_PRAYER"],"tags":["imagination","faith","creation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-010","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 4 — Controlled Reverie","quote_original":"If you do not control your imagination in the reverie, your imagination will control you.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ATTENTION"],"tags":["imagination","reverie","control"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-011","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 4 — Controlled Reverie","quote_original":"To pray successfully you must have clearly defined objectives. You must know what you want before you can ask for it. You must know what you want before you can feel that you have it, and prayer is the feeling of the fulfilled desire.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["DESIRE","FEELING"],"tags":["prayer","objective","wish-fulfilled"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-012","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 4 — Controlled Reverie","quote_original":"When you emerge from prayer you no longer seek, for you have—if you have prayed correctly—subconsciously assumed the reality of the state sought.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["prayer","assumption","completion"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-013","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 5 — Law of Thought Transmission","quote_original":"To think is to speak low; to speak is to think aloud.","primary_topic":"INNER_CONVERSATION","secondary_topics":["THOUGHT"],"tags":["thinking","speech","inner-conversation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-014","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 5 — Law of Thought Transmission","quote_original":"Your beliefs, your fixed attitudes of mind, constantly modify your consciousness as it is reflected on the mirror of your mind. Your consciousness, modified by your beliefs, objectifies itself in the conditions of your world. To change your world, you must first change your conception of it.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["BELIEF","CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["beliefs","world","self-concept"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-015","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 5 — Law of Thought Transmission","quote_original":"Subjective words—subconscious assumptions—awaken what they affirm.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["INNER_CONVERSATION"],"tags":["assumption","subconscious","words"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-016","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 5 — Law of Thought Transmission","quote_original":"Whatever state has your attention holds your life.","primary_topic":"ATTENTION","secondary_topics":["STATES"],"tags":["attention","state","life"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-017","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 5 — Law of Thought Transmission","quote_original":"Some people are self-impressed best by visual images, others by mental sounds, and still others by mental actions. The form of mental activity which allows the whole power of your attention to be focused in one chosen direction is the one to cultivate until you can bring all to play on your objective at the same time.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ATTENTION","INNER_CONVERSATION"],"tags":["visualization","mental-sound","mental-action","attention"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-018","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 6 — Good Tidings","quote_original":"The seemingly harmless habit of “talking to yourself” is the most fruitful form of prayer.","primary_topic":"INNER_CONVERSATION","secondary_topics":["FAITH_PRAYER"],"tags":["self-talk","prayer","inner-conversation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-019","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 7 — The Greatest Prayer","quote_original":"Imagination is the beginning of creation. You imagine what you desire, and then you believe it to be true.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["BELIEF","DESIRE"],"tags":["imagination","creation","belief"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-020","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 7 — The Greatest Prayer","quote_original":"A mood attracts its affinities but it does not create what it attracts.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["STATES"],"tags":["mood","affinity","state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"PAB-CUR-021","corpus_id":"B005","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Prayer, The Art Of Believing","source_year":1945,"source_slug":"prayer_the_art_of_believing","source_section":"Chapter 7 — The Greatest Prayer","quote_original":"Creation is finished. You call your creation into being by feeling the reality of the state you would call.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["FEELING","SPIRITUAL"],"tags":["creation","feeling","state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_prayer_the_art_of_believing.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
